  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Provision of life-saving quality education emergency services, and WASH services to the most vulnerable, crisis-affected girls and boys, including those with disabilities</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of this $2 million UNICEF project is to provide life-saving emergency education services as well water and sanitary hygiene (WASH) support to crisis-affected people. To that end, UNICEF will rehabilitate critical water and sanitation infrastructure, distribute essential hygiene items, and conduct hygiene promotion activities to support 35,000 people, including 9,800 women, 8750 girls and 700 people with disabilities, in the WASH sector. UNICEF will also set up temporary learning spaces and distribute dignity kits and learning supplies to facilitate access to education for 18,692, including 8,365 boys, 8,364 girls and 1,714 people with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
